### Origen permitido
GET http://localhost:1337/health
Origin: http://localhost:3456

### Origen NO permitido
GET http://localhost:1337/health
Origin: http://sitio-random.com

### ================================
### VARIABLES - Ajustar según .env
### ================================
@baseUrl = http://localhost:1337/
@allowedOrigin = http://localhost:3456
@notAllowedOrigin = http://sitio-random.com


### ================================
### 1. HEALTHCHECK
### ================================

### 1.1 Healthcheck - origen permitido -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

### 1.2 Healthcheck - origen NO permitido -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Origin: {{notAllowedOrigin}}

### 1.3 Healthcheck - sin header Origin -> depende de tu config CORS actual
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### ================================
### 2. 404 - RUTA INEXISTENTE
### ================================

### 2.1 Ruta random -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/esto-no-existe
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}


### ================================
### 3. POST /contact/msg - CASOS VALIDOS
### ================================

### 3.1 Mensaje válido -> 201 + mail real enviado
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{
  "name": "Agustín Test",
  "email": "agustin.test@example.com",
  "message": "Hola, este es un mensaje de prueba end-to-end para confirmar que todo el flujo funciona."
}


### ================================
### 4. POST /contact/msg - VALIDACIONES (deberían dar 400)
### ================================

### 4.1 Falta el campo "name" -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{
  "email": "agustin.test@example.com",
  "message": "Mensaje sin nombre, debería fallar la validación."
}

### 4.2 Falta el campo "email" -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{
  "name": "Agustín Test",
  "message": "Mensaje sin email, debería fallar la validación."
}

### 4.3 Falta el campo "message" -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{
  "name": "Agustín Test",
  "email": "agustin.test@example.com"
}

### 4.4 Email con formato inválido -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{
  "name": "Agustín Test",
  "email": "esto-no-es-un-email",
  "message": "El email de este request no tiene formato válido."
}

### 4.5 Name demasiado corto (< 2 caracteres) -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{
  "name": "A",
  "email": "agustin.test@example.com",
  "message": "El nombre de este request tiene solo un caracter."
}

### 4.6 Message demasiado corto (< 5 caracteres) -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{
  "name": "Agustín Test",
  "email": "agustin.test@example.com",
  "message": "Hi"
}

### 4.7 Body vacío -> 400 (deberían saltar los 3 errores de "required" juntos)
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{}


### ================================
### 5. POST /contact/msg - CORS
### ================================

### 5.1 Origen NO permitido -> 403 (no debería llegar ni a validar el body)
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{notAllowedOrigin}}

{
  "name": "Bot Malicioso",
  "email": "bot@spam.com",
  "message": "Este request viene de un origen no autorizado."
}


### ================================
### 6. POST /contact/msg - RATE LIMITING
### ================================

### 6.1 Request de prueba para repetir manualmente -> 429 al superar el límite
POST {{baseUrl}}api/v1/contact/msg
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{allowedOrigin}}

{
  "name": "Rate Limit Test",
  "email": "agustin.test@example.com",
  "message": "Repetir este request varias veces seguidas para gatillar el rate limit."
}